Mojo Spy

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
On the eve of the Firecracker Festival, Dorothy's Fortunate Egg robot
turned Boss Feng's Grain and Oil Shop into a popcorn shop.
But Boss Feng accused Firecracker Long, her old nemesis, of doing it all.
The conflict between them kept escalating.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:47,079
Heart Ore

13
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:47,740
Excuse me, excuse me!

14
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:48,200
Wait for me!

15
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,079
Wait for me!

16
00:01:49,079 --> 00:01:57,200
Popcorn all over the ground!

17
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:09,420
Excuse me.

18
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,180
这里需要侦探吗？

19
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:14,420
We need it!

20
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:16,560
You're the one who did it!

21
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,620
What? I did that?

22
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:19,300
I said it wasn't me!

23
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:19,939
You still won't admit it?

24
00:02:19,939 --> 00:02:21,360
You're so heartless.

25
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,300
Still trying to deny it?

26
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:23,860
It was you who did it

27
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:24,520
Stop pretending

28
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,520
Who's pretending?

29
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,300
Cut the act

30
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:27,240
I'm not acting!

31
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:27,939
It's you!

32
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:29,780
Are you still trying to deny it?

33
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:30,540
Look at this

34
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,780
Look what you've done to my shop!

35
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:38,080
So that's what happened

36
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:41,580
Everything in my shop

37
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:42,860
has all turned into popcorn

38
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:47,780
Thankfully, this fortune-bringing

39
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:49,080
Firecracker Festival Fortunate Egg is still fine

40
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:52,220
I'll keep it safe forever

41
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:54,080
Maybe it'll ward off the bad luck

42
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,380
someone has brought me

43
00:02:55,379 --> 00:02:58,840
But what does that have to do with me?

44
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:01,639
Even if it wasn't you

45
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:03,019
Don't you have any sympathy?

46
00:03:03,019 --> 00:03:05,240
You say *I* have no sympathy?

47
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,819
I was the first one who ran in here to save you!

48
00:03:07,819 --> 00:03:09,840
You're so ungrateful!

49
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,439
Who are you calling ungrateful?

50
00:03:11,439 --> 00:03:12,400
Say that again!

51
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,400
What did I say wrong?

52
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,120
Say that again.

53
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,659
I was the first one to run in and save you.

54
00:03:15,659 --> 00:03:17,180
I can't hear you clearly.

55
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:22,519
You heartless thing!

56
00:03:22,519 --> 00:03:23,680
The first to run in and save you
Your sympathy really makes me sick

57
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:29,240
It really is here after all.
You make me sad—you've got no heart.
You've really chilled my heart.

58
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:54,800
Jerk!

59
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:58,480
Love
Dreams

60
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,680
Love
Dreams

61
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:03,519
I never would have thought...

62
00:05:03,519 --> 00:05:05,720
Thy-thy has slipped up twice, too.

63
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,199
Such a simple thing, made so complicated.

64
00:05:08,199 --> 00:05:10,519
How dare you call her Thy-thy?!

65
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:14,439
Oh, what a surprise!

66
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:17,060
I know this was definitely an accident.

67
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:19,699
If Lord Dorothy makes a move again

68
00:05:19,699 --> 00:05:21,160
It's sure to succeed.

69
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:23,900
Lord Eye

70
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:26,080
My charm is my promise.

71
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:27,080
Tomorrow night.

72
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:29,100
Tomorrow night, we'll pull it off.

73
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:31,720
Very good.

74
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:40,360
Dear viewers

75
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,280
Late last night.

76
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,379
Another transformation at the Grain and Oil Shop.

77
00:05:43,379 --> 00:05:44,879
But this time it wasn't popcorn.

78
00:05:44,879 --> 00:05:46,800
It was a grand fireworks show.

79
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,680
Don't cry.

80
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:51,300
Did you do this?

81
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:51,780
Yes.

82
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:52,780
No.

83
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:53,459
Yes.

84
00:05:53,459 --> 00:05:56,259
You're way out of line!

85
00:05:56,259 --> 00:05:57,199
A grown man

86
00:05:57,199 --> 00:05:59,160
How could you bully a weak woman like this?

87
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,800
How could you do this?

88
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,920
I'm innocent!

89
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:03,900
So many Fortunate Eggs!

90
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,879
Could it really be Firecracker Long?

91
00:06:05,879 --> 00:06:09,160
I'm innocent! Innocent of what?

92
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,860
Suddenly there were lots of Fortunate Eggs.

93
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:12,199
So many, so many.

94
00:06:12,199 --> 00:06:13,860
I really am innocent!

95
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:15,300
I'm innocent!

96
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,399
So many Fortunate Eggs!

97
00:06:16,399 --> 00:06:17,620
So many, so many Fortunate Eggs!

98
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:18,699
Then they suddenly exploded!

99
00:06:18,699 --> 00:06:24,959
I'm innocent!

100
00:06:24,959 --> 00:06:25,840
Fortunate Eggs! That's it!

101
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:28,819
Boss Feng's beloved Firecracker Festival Fortunate Egg is gone.

102
00:06:28,819 --> 00:06:30,720
Something's off here.

103
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,420
Looks like we should contact Hawxing.

104
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:35,399
Contact him?

105
00:06:35,399 --> 00:06:36,620
No way.

106
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:46,459
Firecracker Festival Fortunate Egg.

107
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:50,320
Did you hear something?

108
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:53,220
No, nothing.

109
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:56,180
It's a signal from this egg.

110
00:06:56,180 --> 00:07:02,640
The Fortunate Egg is sending a signal?

111
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:06,860
This egg could be the breakthrough.

112
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:52,460
Help!

113
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:58,460
Firecracker Long?

114
00:07:58,460 --> 00:08:00,460
The truth is out.

115
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:02,460
I've been released.

116
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:04,460
Let's get you out of here.

117
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,460
Wait.

118
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:37,960
My Feng.

119
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,280
Long, darling.

120
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,019
This is...

121
00:08:41,019 --> 00:08:42,900
I've been keeping it all along.

122
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:46,240
This is the wedding gift you gave me.

123
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,419
The Love Ore.

124
00:08:48,419 --> 00:08:55,039
This really is the Love Ore.

125
00:08:55,039 --> 00:08:59,320
This is a family heirloom.

126
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:02,039
Then why is it with Grain Feng?

127
00:09:02,039 --> 00:09:07,019
Because she's my wife.

128
00:09:07,019 --> 00:09:11,820
Back then, she wanted to open a grain and oil shop.

129
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:13,600
I wanted to open a firecracker shop.

130
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:16,360
So we had a falling out.

131
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:19,200
Thank you for saving me.

132
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,420
I'll pass this ore on to you.

133
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:25,420
Actually, that day I wanted to give you a bundle of fireworks.

134
00:09:25,420 --> 00:09:26,600
To cheer you up.

135
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,360
But I never expected...

136
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,840
I know.

137
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:32,139
Let's make up.

138
00:09:32,139 --> 00:09:34,560
Then you have to promise me one condition.

139
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,060
What condition?

140
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:38,660
You have to make me popcorn every day.

141
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:42,720
Okay, okay!

142
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,720
Yay! Yay! Yay!

143
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:19,980
Saying goodbye to today always makes us feel lost.

144
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:27,820
Look at tomorrow, waving to me from the horizon.

145
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:35,440
Every day, sunrise to sunset, time spins, and we dream of more.

146
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:40,500
Looking forward to every second, every moment of life.

147
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:47,220
My bright eyes are sparkling.

148
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:50,600
A smile that greets the sun.

149
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:55,799
Stepping quietly at the screaming crossroads.